5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447327 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that by definition, the square root is always zero or positive, never negative.\n\nSo, the square root comes out to\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{(-100)^{2}}=\\sqrt{{100}^{2}}=100.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447328 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447324 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447328 #edb/ref 1069 "q-99138" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447328 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447328 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $(\\sqrt{7})^{2}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447328 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a6920c8a-7064-5177-94ae-b7e5a0869cee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447328 #edb/ref 1074 "The number in the square root is non-negative, so the square and the square root cancel each other out.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n(\\sqrt{7})^{2}=7.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447329 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447323 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447329 #edb/ref 1069 "q-69747" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447329 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447329 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $\\sqrt{{(-9)}^{2}}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447329 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bab3fe97-7845-5d24-a55f-a0948cbbb2ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447329 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that by definition, the square root is always zero or positive, never negative.\n\nSo, the square root comes out to\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{(-9)^{2}}=\\sqrt{{9}^{2}}=9.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
